{%- comment -%}
  Hartwick Atelier — availability, stated as a fact.

  Aloha, 3 September 2026, lists availability among the things that stay inside
  the product panel — and, in the same letter, removes scarcity language from
  the site: "We do not want to turn that reality into scarcity language that
  pressures customers into buying quickly."

  So this line is deliberately narrow. It says whether the piece can be bought
  and, where Hartwick has written one, how. It never counts remaining stock,
  never says "only 2 left", "selling fast" or "almost gone", and never runs a
  countdown. Luxe's own `inventory` block does exactly those things, which is
  why this is not that block.

    hartwick.availability_note   "Through The Register"   — Hartwick's own words
    otherwise                     derived from Shopify's real stock state

  Terminology (CLAUDE.md): Reserve is Phase 2 and is not offered here.

  Usage (inside a main-product custom_liquid block):
    {% render 'ha-availability', label: 'Availability' %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign note = product.metafields.hartwick.availability_note

  if note == blank
    if product.available
      assign note = 'Available now'
    else
      assign note = 'Not currently available'
    endif
  endif

  assign row_label = label | default: 'Availability'
-%}

<div class="ha-pdp__availability ha-record">
  <span class="ha-pdp__availability-label">{{ row_label }}</span>
  <span class="ha-pdp__availability-value">{{ note }}</span>
</div>
